Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:36:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Preview: no box behind the Plate rating; the dark tiers shade
 the card's corner instead (Parker, 11 Oct 2026)

Parker, on the preview: "I don't know if I really want that box above the rating. It's super unnecessary."

The box is gone on every tier (no background, padding or ::before on .fc .rt). Gold and silver figures read 7:1 on
the card as they are. Without the box the contrast audit failed 17 texts, all on the four dark tiers, whose fills are
mid tones where no colour reaches 7:1 (elite: cyan 4.3:1, white 6.4:1); those tiers shade the card's top left corner
instead, a soft radial shade at the box's old darkness, clipped inside the inner keyline, under the photo and the
figures, with no edges. The contrast audit with the real fonts: 0 offenders on 42 screens.

Tests: tests/app-images.js section 4 (no box; the shade on the dark tiers only; the figure's audited band inside the
shade's solid part and its clip), tests/app-contrast.js P3 and C16, fplgg/tools/preview/check-images.js. BUGS #50,
the run report's follow-up, ROADMAP and CLAUDE.md updated.

